  "props": {
    "title": "Millcreek tree canopy",
    "snippet": "Tree canopy cover by ownership zone, with lidar tree crowns and treetops by height, over imagery of Millcreek, Utah. Unvalidated planning estimates; not surveyed or field-verified.",
    "description": "<p><b>Planning estimates.</b> The layers in this map are unvalidated estimates derived from lidar by City of Millcreek GIS. They have not been surveyed, engineered or checked in the field. Use them for planning, screening and display, not for legal, engineering, property-boundary, permitting or code-compliance decisions.</p><p>At city scale: canopy cover (vegetation at least 2 m tall, as a share of the area the lidar observed) for each ownership zone; click a zone for its figure, bounds and the October 19 comparison. Zoom in past 1:20,000 for the tree crowns and, from 1:10,000, the treetops, coloured and sized by treetop height. The lidar hillshade is blended over the imagery (soft light).</p><p>Treetops and crowns are unvalidated automatic detections; about 6% of treetops carry an unreviewed SUSPECT flag.</p><p><b>Treetop height (crowns and treetops):</b> <span style='color:#D9F0A3'>\u25a0</span> 2 to 5 m &nbsp; <span style='color:#ADDD8E'>\u25a0</span> 5 to 10 m &nbsp; <span style='color:#78C679'>\u25a0</span> 10 to 15 m &nbsp; <span style='color:#31A354'>\u25a0</span> 15 to 20 m &nbsp; <span style='color:#006837'>\u25a0</span> 20 m and over; larger treetop dots are taller trees.</p><p>Crowns and treetops are vector tiles: they draw but have no pop-ups. A legend cannot read a vector tile style, so each is grouped with a small key layer that carries its classes into the legend.</p><p><b>Lidar source.</b> The 2023 Salt Lake Valley QL1 lidar (USGS project UT_2023SaltLakeCo_C24, USGS 3D Elevation Program), flown on October 7, November 2 and November 4, 2023. Quality level 1 means at least 8 pulses per square metre and a vertical accuracy (RMSEz) of 10 cm or better on open, non-vegetated ground under the USGS specification; the vendor's own accuracy report for this project has not been reviewed for these products. For these products the building and vegetation classes of the points were refined; the ground class was not changed. All products are gridded at 0.5 m.</p><p><b>Coordinates and heights.</b> Built in NAD83(2011) / UTM zone 12N (EPSG 6341), metres, and taken to WGS84 / Web Mercator for ArcGIS Online with the transformation WGS_1984_(ITRF08)_To_NAD_1983_2011. Every layer in the Millcreek LiDAR 2023 set uses this same transformation, so the layers line up with each other and with Esri's basemaps to a few centimetres; without it they would sit about 1.2 m apart. Elevations are NAVD88 (Geoid18) in <b>metres</b>; heights are metres above the lidar bare-earth terrain.</p><p><b>Questions or corrections:</b> City of Millcreek GIS. The processing records (scripts, checks and run logs) are kept by City of Millcreek GIS.</p>",
    "tags": [
      "Millcreek",
      "Utah",
      "Salt Lake County",
      "lidar",
      "2023 lidar",
      "3DEP",
      "planning estimate",
      "tree canopy",
      "urban forest",
      "trees",
      "treetops",
      "crowns",
      "web map"
    ],
    "accessInformation": "City of Millcreek GIS; 2023 Salt Lake Valley QL1 lidar (USGS 3DEP)",
    "licenseInfo": "<p>These data are unvalidated planning estimates produced by City of Millcreek GIS from 2023 lidar. They are not surveyed, engineered or field-verified, and must not be used to determine property boundaries or ownership, building or site design, engineering, flood or drainage design, code compliance (including building height), or any legal or regulatory determination. They are provided as is, without warranty of accuracy, completeness or fitness for any purpose; check conditions on the ground before relying on them. Credit \"City of Millcreek GIS; 2023 Salt Lake Valley QL1 lidar (USGS 3DEP)\" when you use or show them.</p>"
  },
